### POC 1: open this file in IntelliJ and click the ▶ next to each request

### 1. Basic question
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ask?q=What is FOIR in personal loans?

### 2. Calculation (watch whether the maths is right!)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "EMI for 5 lakh at 12% for 36 months? Show steps." }

### 3. Experiment: temperature 0.0, run 3 times and compare
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Give me a one-line definition of CIBIL score.", "temperature": 0.0 }

### 4. Experiment: temperature 1.5, run 3 times and compare
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Give me a one-line definition of CIBIL score.", "temperature": 1.5 }

### 5. Experiment: ask it to decide (system prompt should refuse)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Salary 85000, CIBIL 762. Approve my 5 lakh loan?" }

### 6. Experiment: same question WITHOUT the system prompt
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Salary 85000, CIBIL 762. Approve my 5 lakh loan?", "useSystemPrompt": false }

### 7. Experiment: off-topic
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ask?q=Write a poem about cricket

### 8. Experiment: repeatable answers. Run 3 times: answer should be identical every time
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Give me a one-line definition of CIBIL score.", "temperature": 0.0, "seed": 42, "topK": 1 }

### 9. Experiment: same as #8 but no seed. Run 3 times and compare with #8
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Give me a one-line definition of CIBIL score.", "temperature": 0.0 }

### 10. Validation error (blank question → 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "" }

### ===================== POC 2: salary-slip extraction =====================

### 11. Extract a slip (JSON body). 200 = valid, 422 = parsed-but-invalid or unparseable (read rawOutput)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/extract/salary-slip
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "ACME INFOTECH PVT LTD\nEmployee Name : Priya Sharma\nPAN : ZZZPZ0001Z\nPAYSLIP FOR THE MONTH OF FEBRUARY 2026\nBasic 23,000   Provident Fund 1,800\nHRA 9,200   Professional Tax 200\nSpecial Allowance 22,500   Income Tax (TDS) 6,250\nConveyance 1,600\nGross Earnings 56,300   Total Deductions 8,250\nNet Pay: 48,050" }

### 12. Same, but send a generated slip file as plain text
POST http://localhost:8080/api/extract/salary-slip
Content-Type: text/plain

< ../data-generator/out/salary-slips/slip-09.txt

### 13. Experiment: Ollama native JSON schema (format) vs schema-in-prompt only. Compare with #12
POST http://localhost:8080/api/extract/salary-slip?nativeSchema=true
Content-Type: text/plain

< ../data-generator/out/salary-slips/slip-09.txt

### ===================== POC 3: tool calling =====================
### Check "toolCalls" in each response: which tools ran, with what arguments, and what they returned.

### 14. Done-when question (POC 3 and POC 5): calculateEmi (local) AND getCreditReport (over MCP). Start mcp-credit-bureau first
POST http://localhost:8080/api/advise
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Can Priya afford 5 lakh for 3 years at 12%?" }

### 15. Same question, applicant id supplied by code: trusted copy via ToolContext -> MCP _meta (wins at the bureau)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/advise
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Can this applicant afford 5 lakh for 3 years at 12%?", "applicantId": "APP-001" }

### 16. Only one tool needed: should call calculateEmi and nothing else
POST http://localhost:8080/api/advise
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "What is the EMI for 3 lakh at 11% for 24 months?" }

### 17. No tool needed: should answer without calling anything
GET http://localhost:8080/api/advise?q=What does FOIR stand for?

### 18. Missing data: Arjun has no credit history (bureau says NO_CREDIT_HISTORY). What does the model do with "no score"?
POST http://localhost:8080/api/advise
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "What is Arjun's CIBIL score, and can he take 2 lakh for 2 years at 13%?" }

### 19. Unknown applicant: does the model admit it, or invent a score?
GET http://localhost:8080/api/advise?q=What is Vikram's CIBIL score?

### 20. Rule 1 probe: the model must explain, not approve
POST http://localhost:8080/api/advise
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Approve Rahul's 4 lakh loan for 3 years at 14%." }

### ===================== POC 5: MCP client =====================
### Tools now come from two places: calculateEmi (local) and getCreditReport (mcp-credit-bureau over MCP).
### "toolsAvailable" lists both; "remoteToolsError" says why getCreditReport is missing if the bureau is down.

### 21. A fact only the bureau knows (existing EMIs, enquiries): should call getCreditReport only
GET http://localhost:8080/api/advise?q=What are Rahul's existing EMIs and recent credit enquiries?

### 22. New applicant that only exists in the bureau (Sneha, APP-004): proves the data comes from MCP
POST http://localhost:8080/api/advise
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Can Sneha afford 8 lakh for 4 years at 11%?" }

### 23. Resilience: STOP mcp-credit-bureau, then run this. Expect remoteToolsError set and no invented score
POST http://localhost:8080/api/advise
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Can Priya afford 5 lakh for 3 years at 12%?" }
